tParkerDev Can you upload a MRP? We can't act on your issue if we can't reproduce it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2639120219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2639774582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101823#issuecomment-2639774582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101823","id":2639774582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dV8N2","user":{"login":"MattParkerDev","id":61717342,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzE3MzQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61717342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev","html_url":"https://github.com/MattParkerDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MattParkerDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-06T13:04:33Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T13:04:33Z","body":"[SkeletonBugRepro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18690259/SkeletonBugRepro.zip)\n\n@rburing Here is a repro\n\nTo run:\nensure C# is built\nenable debug visible collision shapes\nrun project\nwalk up to blue humanoid and touch with bat in hand to activate ragdoll\nobserve mesh glitching away from collision shapes\nIf you wish to find the scene in Game.tscn, look up 😅\n\nNote:\nI am using GodotPhysics, and physics interpolation enabled - I may have misreported this as a GodotJolt issue.\n\nAlso, I don't know whether it was something I did wrong, but I had major problems copying this project to another folder and running it, to ensure it works as an MRP (building it failed). I don't know if godot is mad because the project name is the same, but I just got a nice \"Your build is busted\" error message popup. Hopefully you have more luck running it 😅","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2639774582/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2641083511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101823#issuecomment-2641083511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101823","id":2641083511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6da7x3","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-06T21:23:41Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T21:46:06Z","body":"Here is a more minimal (also non-C#) reproduction project: [SkeletonBugRepro-more-minimal.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18697636/SkeletonBugRepro-more-minimal.zip)\n\nJust applying an impulse to the rigid body and starting simulation of the PhysicalBoneSimulator3D is enough to trigger the bug. A workaround is to turn off physics interpolation of the Skeleton3D node. (After selecting the Skeleton3D node in the scene tree, go to Node > Physics Interpolation > Mode in the inspector on the right, and set the property to Off.)\n\nI'll investigate how to fix this. cc @lawnjelly @TokageItLab ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2641083511/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2647121379","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101823#issuecomment-2647121379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101823","id":2647121379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dx93j","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T07:11:45Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T09:28:04Z","body":"Just having a look now.\n\nIt's easier to see when you drop physics tick per second to 10 or so.\n \nUPDATE:\nSeems to be something to do with the `apply_central_impulse`:\n```\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tawait get_tree().physics_frame\n\tapply_central_impulse(Vector3.FORWARD * 200)\n\tphysical_bone_simulator_3d.physical_bones_start_simulation()\n```\nThis is sending the ZombieParent (and the capsule mesh instance indicator) far into the distance, while the ragdoll itself is staying in place.\nMaybe the ragdoll is being specified relative to the `ZombieParent` physics position, rather than the interpolated position, hence is jumping around in rendered position according to what the interpolation fraction is.\n\nStill looking.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79bb63de-ec36-4894-88ca-2e12e3118478\n\nYeah you can see here the ragdoll is being affected by the transform of the parent.\n\nUPDATE:\nI'm not super familiar with this implementation of ragdoll, but am suspecting this may require converting to be physics interpolation aware in order to work \"properly\".\n\nThis is likely to be a special case like particle systems.\n\nEssentially for physics interpolation to work \"correctly\", each moving part must maintain a previous and current transform (on the tick) and be interpolated on the frame for rendering. The ragdoll (as far as I can see) updates on the physics tick, but only stores a single global xform for each bone.\n\nFor most simple objects the magic for interpolation is done for you in `VisualServer`, but it could be here the bones would need to maintain previous and current xforms, deal with resetting etc, because they update the skin. This is a general problem with skinned meshes - for regular animation the solution is simply to update the skinned mesh on the frame (rather than the tick), but for physically controlled skinned meshes we can't do that so easily as it might disrupt the simulation.\n\nFor now I would recommend switching off interpolation for the branch. It would be nice to enforce this for ragdoll, but `Skeleton3D` I believe is reused for non-ragdoll stuff, so you may have to do this via `PhysicalBoneSimulator3D` turning off interpolation in its `Skeleton3D` when active (via `set_physics_interpolation_mode(Node::PHYSICS_INTERPOLATION_MODE_OFF)`.\n\n(_More precisely, it is actually the skinned mesh `alpha_joints` and `alpha_surface` that needs interpolation off, but they will inherit it from `Skeleton3D` if you turn that off._)\n\n### To get it to work properly\nThis may not be that big a job (but sometimes there can be unforeseen complications), and might require some testing in the wild to work out the bugs.\nEssentially I think you'd need to:\n* Store a prev and curr xform for each bone\n* Manage the pumping of the current to previous on the physics tick (before the new data is applied)\n* On the frame, interpolate the bone transforms using the interpolation fraction, and only update the skin at this stage\n* Handle resets as with other nodes\n* Fallback to just storing current xforms etc when physics interpolation is off\n\nIt may also be possible to add some bodges to account for the gross effects of the parent xform (like setting the nodes to ignore parent xform and be in true global space), but this will likely end up with the same situation as turning off interpolation.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2647121379/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2729264831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101823#issuecomment-2729264831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101823","id":2729264831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6irUa_","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-17T12:13:36Z","updated_at":"2025-03-17T12:13:36Z","body":"Just an update, the new FTI in #104269 helps but this issue likely needs some specific code to handle physics interpolation properly (is is a special case), and is out of scope for the general change.\n\nUntil then I still recommend setting `physics_interpolation_mode` to OFF for these branches.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2729264831/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]